        "answer": "The F-14 Tomcat uses two afterburning turbofans, while the F-16 Fighting Falcon is a single-engine aircraft. The F-14A uses two Pratt & Whitney TF30-P-414A engines (20,900 lb each), and the F-14B/D uses two General Electric F110-GE-400 engines (27,000 lb each). The F-16C uses one afterburning turbofan: either a General Electric F110-GE-129 on the Block 50 (29,500 lbf) or a Pratt & Whitney F100-PW-229 on the Block 52.",
        "ids": [
